ok   a gzip body is inflated once and the same String is returned every time
ok   x-gzip is gzip too
ok   embedded NUL bytes survive the inflate
ok   an empty gzip member inflates to an empty body
ok   a multi-member gzip file is inflated whole
ok   bytes after the last member that are not a member make the body undecodable
ok   a body that is not gzip, or too short to be, is undecodable before anything is read
ok   a corrupt member (a flipped byte in the deflate data) is undecodable
ok   a truncated member is undecodable
ok   a body one byte over the limit is refused, one at the limit passes
ok   a trailer that lies small changes nothing: the inflater measures the output
ok   a zip bomb is refused at the ceiling: 20 MB of zeros, small on the wire, against a 1 MiB limit
ok   a decode error is not cached: every call raises again, and a later larger limit succeeds
ok   a cached body is checked against a smaller limit asked for later
ok   GzipFFI.gunzip refuses a limit it cannot represent
